was relocated) than everything seems to be fine - except i have still problems
with one bus on a double-SCSI-controller.

6 disks on one bus of the double-controller reports problems - i connected them
to another controller (slower SCSI).

I suggest the controller is defective after power failure 2 weeks ago.

Thanks to Danielle Georgette which suggests the prpasswd is the origin of the
problem - it was not. And william_f_fiore_jr who told me:

I recently had a similar situ w/ lockd disappearing...but system still running and unusable.
I shutdown all the cluster nodes (I had to 'crash dump' the nodes w/ control-P).
Then none of the nodes would boot up.....It turned out that a disk controller was in a 1/2 on - 1/2 off
state....reseting the disk controller by plugging a VT100 into it.....fixed it.
I would have removed power from the systems (which would have cleared the 1/2on-off state) but
the system had been powered on for more than 8 years.....I was afraid that the disks would not spin back up....
so It took 1/2 a day to find and reset the disk controllar with the 1/2on-off situ

			Thanks, Harald Baumgartner
