Hello,

I was successful in installing freetype2 using HP's tachometer perl
script.  Martin Adolfson was kind to inform me that HP had changed the
URL for the tachometer content but had not update the script.  Following
are the changes which need to be made at the beginning of the tachometer
script:

$gconfig{REMOTEHOST}="h30097.www3.hp.com";
$gconfig{REMOTEPORT}="80";
$gconfig{REMOTEPATH}="/demos/ossc";

For those who do not know what tachometer is, please refer to the
following URL:
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/demos/ossc/html/OSSCV51B.htm

Regards,
Bill Antoniadis

>Hello,
>
>I've been, for many days, trying to compile freetype 2.1.10 for Tru64.
>Unfortunately, I am getting libtool errors complaining that the "print
>-r" cannot be found and I have been unsuccessful in working around that.
